Atlas","/farmland-atlas/kansas/greenwood-county"],["ARC or PLC in Greenwood County","/arc-plc/kansas/greenwood-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years. In 2025 that pair landed at 49% of normal on the middle of the grids, while June to July came in at 140%. Grid 21434 had its driest year in 1956, at 49% of normal.</p>"}
